---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const toc = [
  { id: 'pin', label: 'Pin' },
  { id: 'velocity', label: '3.2.0–6.5.0' },
  { id: 'policy', label: 'Minor bumps' },
  { id: 'added-650', label: 'Added in 6.5.0' },
  { id: 'read', label: 'Where to read next' },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  title="REA changelog for operators (3.2.0–6.5.0) | rea.run"
  description="Operator changelog for rea-agents from 3.2.0 through npm 6.5.0, with publish times and the always-bump-minor caveat. Not a paste of every PR."
  path="/changelog/"
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-12">
    <div class="docs-layout">
      <aside class="docs-toc hidden md:block">
        <p class="section-kicker mb-3">On this page</p>
        {toc.map((item) => <a href={`#${item.id}`}>{item.label}</a>)}
      </aside>
      <article class="prose-page">
        <p class="badge">Changelog</p>
        <h1 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[var(--color-ink)] sm:text-4xl">What shipped, through rea-agents 6.5.0</h1>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-base leading-7 text-[var(--color-muted)]">
          Community index of GitHub releases from <strong>3.2.0</strong> (2026-10-03) through <strong>6.5.0</strong> (2026-10-14).
          Times are release <code>published_at</code> in UTC. npm <code>latest</code> checked on <strong>2026-10-15</strong> was <strong>6.5.0</strong>.
          Feature sentences are shortened from those release bodies. The upgrade procedure lives on the <a href="/docs/breaking/">breaking-change runbook</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 id="pin">Pin this site teaches</h2>
        <pre><code>npx -y rea-agents@6.5.0 setup
npx -y rea-agents@6.5.0 doctor --json</code></pre>
        <p>
          Node engines for that tarball: <code>^22.19.0 || ^24.11.0 || &gt;=26.0.0</code>.
          MCP Registry id: <code>io.github.morluto/rea</code> (the registry installs the same npm package; it is not a second artifact).
          Client IDs: <a href="/docs/clients/">6.5.0 matrix</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 id="velocity">Release index</h2>
        <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-6">
          <table class="compare-table">
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Version</th><th>Published (UTC)</th><th>Operator note</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td><a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/releases/tag/rea-agents-3.2.0">3.2.0</a></td>
                <td>2026-10-03 16:43</td>
                <td>Native investigation features (#486).</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/releases/tag/rea-agents-3.2.1">3.2.1</a></td>
                <td>2026-10-03 19:58</td>
                <td>Patch: tolerate npm registry propagation delay. No feature list.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/releases/tag/rea-agents-4.0.0">4.0.0</a></td>
                <td>2026-10-05 18:29</td>
                <td>Breaking. Unscoped setup refreshes only existing REA registrations (<code>--all-detected</code> for every detected client). Replay, permission, and several tracing tools removed. Managed comparison metadata adds exact-signature matching.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/releases/tag/rea-agents-4.0.1">4.0.1</a></td>
                <td>2026-10-05 18:54</td>
                <td>Patch: allow npm propagation time. No feature list.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/releases/tag/rea-agents-4.1.0">4.1.0</a></td>
                <td>2026-10-06 17:57</td>
                <td>Static Android via headless JADX (#738), firmware Binwalk/Unblob, IDA read-only MCP (#754), Command Code setup (#645), more Ghidra surfaces including Windows x64 read-only.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/releases/tag/rea-agents-5.0.0">5.0.0</a></td>
                <td>2026-10-07 17:26</td>
                <td>Breaking: Android analysis needs a full JDK 17+ with the compiler module. Also Apple/Android inventory graphs, browser capture tracing, Wakaru recovery. Upstream install notes at the 6.4.0 tag describe this checkpoint as 133 MCP tools.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/releases/tag/rea-agents-6.0.0">6.0.0</a></td>
                <td>2026-10-08 09:40</td>
                <td>Breaking: MCP filesystem inputs require absolute host paths (#948, #1004). CLI relative paths remain. <a href="/docs/breaking/#paths">Steps</a>.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/releases/tag/rea-agents-6.1.0">6.1.0</a></td>
                <td>2026-10-09 01:08</td>
                <td>Breaking for Hopper: ECMAScript Unicode regex, five-second deadline, <code>set_current_document</code> removed. <a href="/docs/breaking/#hopper">Steps</a>.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/releases/tag/rea-agents-6.2.0">6.2.0</a></td>
                <td>2026-10-09 16:51</td>
                <td>Breaking Evidence contract. Success payload is the record; read <code>normalized_result</code>. <code>always-bump-minor</code> called out in the migration guide. <a href="/docs/breaking/#evidence">Steps</a>.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/releases/tag/rea-agents-6.3.0">6.3.0</a></td>
                <td>2026-10-09 23:56</td>
                <td>Breaking captures: producer accounting and transaction identity required. Do not synthesize missing web-diff dimensions. <a href="/docs/breaking/#captures">Steps</a>.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/releases/tag/rea-agents-6.4.0">6.4.0</a></td>
                <td>2026-10-11 03:58</td>
                <td>Android ADB lane, caller-started JEB MCP, Pi / Hermes / Qwen Code setup, compact MCP schemas, large Evidence views. Breaking: <code>network.websocket_connections</code> replaces <code>network.websocket_events</code>. <a href="/docs/breaking/#sockets">Steps</a>.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/releases/tag/rea-agents-6.5.0">6.5.0</a></td>
                <td>2026-10-14 12:32</td>
                <td>Current npm latest (checked 2026-10-15). Body date 2026-10-13. JS selection / retained Evidence paging; packet/signal/HAR/QUIC/SAZ; SQLite (Node ≥24.15 or 26+); WASM/Rust/Electron fuses; new clients (Qoder, Trae, ZCode, dsh, kimi, droid, workbuddy). Breaking: null <code>attached</code>/source names; <code>--filter-output</code> null; call-graph <code>{"{"} graph, limitations {"}"}</code>; ADB <code>replace_requested</code>. Release footer: 893 commits / 529 PRs. <a href="/docs/breaking/#nulls">Steps</a>.</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p>
          Seven tags from 3.2.0 (3 Oct) through 6.0.0 (8 Oct), then 6.1.0–6.4.0 on 9–11 Oct, then 6.5.0 on 14 Oct.
          That pace is why a floating install in CI is a behavior change, not a refresh.
        </p>

        <h2 id="policy">How to read a minor bump</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Open the GitHub release for the version you will install. Confirm <code>published_at</code> before you quote it.</li>
          <li>If the body contains <code>BREAKING CHANGES</code>, follow <a href="/docs/breaking/">the runbook</a> even when the bump is only minor. 6.2 states that <code>always-bump-minor</code> includes breaking releases.</li>
          <li>Refresh MCP tool definitions and restart the client. A new package does not update a server that is already running.</li>
          <li>Keep saved Evidence, snapshots, and captures until a regenerated file has been checked. Fresh analysis does not rewrite what an older capture proved.</li>
          <li>Re-run <code>doctor --json</code> on the pin and store the output with the ticket.</li>
        </ol>

        <h2 id="added-650">Added in npm 6.5.0</h2>
        <p>
          Factory Droid (<code>droid</code>), DeepSeek Harness (<code>dsh</code>), Qoder (<code>qoder</code>), Trae (<code>trae</code>), ZCode (<code>zcode</code>), Kimi Code (<code>kimi</code>), and WorkBuddy (<code>workbuddy</code>) ship in the 6.5.0 supported-agents table.
          DeepSeek is included from 6.5.0; live Trae and DeepSeek API integration remain unverified upstream.
          Confirm with <code>setup --dry-run</code> and <code>doctor --client &lt;id&gt; --json</code>. Full table: <a href="/docs/clients/">client matrix</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Pi, Hermes, and Qwen Code already shipped in 6.4.0 (17 IDs). 6.5.0 expands the matrix to 24 <code>--client</code> values. Grok Bot remains a manual hosted connector, not a setup row.
        </p>

        <h2 id="read">Where to read next</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/docs/breaking/">Upgrade runbook, 6.0–6.5.0</a></li>
          <li><a href="/blog/rea-agents-6-4-0/">6.4.0 operator guide</a> — ADB, JEB, compact schema, Evidence views</li>
          <li><a href="/docs/install/">Install</a> · <a href="/docs/clients/">clients</a> · <a href="/docs/jeb/">JEB</a> · <a href="/docs/android-adb/">Android ADB</a></li>
          <li><a href="/showcase/aegis-totp/">Aegis login-code study</a>, pinned to <code>rea-agents@6.4.0</code></li>
        </ul>

        <footer class="mt-12 border-t border-[var(--color-line)] pt-6 text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)] not-prose">
          <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider">Sources</p>
          <ol class="mt-3 list-decimal space-y-1 pl-5 text-xs">
            <li><a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/releases" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">GitHub releases for morluto/rea</a> — publish times in the table</li>
            <li><a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/rea-agents" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">npm rea-agents</a> — latest 6.5.0 on 2026-10-15</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/blob/rea-agents-6.5.0/docs/migration-6.2.md" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">docs/migration-6.2.md at rea-agents-6.5.0</a></li>
          </ol>
          <p class="mt-4"><a class="quiet-link" href="/compliance/">Compliance</a></p>
        </footer>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
